#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184070 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/id #uuid "10cc01a6-af19-5340-9743-ade4d5e252dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5425" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 5$ matrix. If $\\mathcal{B}= \\{\\mathbf{b_1}, \\mathbf{b_2}, \\mathbf{b_3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$, find $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $\\mathcal{B}$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\textrm{rank}(A) = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184071 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "78547385-d46f-5a2a-bfc1-39e040208ca0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5426" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and  ![](images/a7/a7171d7bdd2b5c79b55ce6bd204e36304640468bd2ad533ac4032cd5a4ddc2ae.svg) \n\nI. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=1$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a $2$-dimensional subspace of $\\Bbb R^3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n![](images/ab/ab1cd4be22e0d3344318108914d506f9fc259446654eefff94a36d38afac3f8b.svg)\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that \n![](images/e7/e7660dfd412f13c5d20dd9e77ec439cdbf2916ebfbccc383d13b5f9ed4032cda.svg) \nwhich means that $\\textrm{nullity}(A) =2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n = 3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\textrm{nullity}(A) = 2 \\neq 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ cannot be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\textrm{rank}(A) = 1,$ we have that $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a $1$-dimensional subspace of $\\Bbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184124 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "9615d8af-b005-5449-be4b-a7487375c98f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9963" :question/problem "Consider a $8 \\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\textrm{rank}(A)=5$ then what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then  \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49f0ab4c-fbd4-51c3-9786-ba43e794d43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269938} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab7efee-6ef8-5fc2-be0d-b51827e71b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270075} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2b29b4-2f81-54f4-bdf7-b58a72a2e8d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270222} {:answer/id #uuid "8396f6d2-ebb9-5380-9151-fc1d01a5a275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270405} {:answer/id #uuid "e405d544-5373-5a6b-ae5a-7133727a2f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e405d544-5373-5a6b-ae5a-7133727a2f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271277} :answer-field/id #uuid "49a3e349-c042-5891-b20b-9ce5fdf20642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0934aa4b-cfbc-551f-aede-b568683fcc43" :question/math-academy-id "q-141228" :question/problem "Consider a $6\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=2,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =8 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4635be5a-a6fe-56a4-8e10-c0910f4f8147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269912} {:answer/id #uuid "576e17c2-77cc-5c9e-8c7f-5cabff8304b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270041} {:answer/id #uuid "8f2da899-b45f-50aa-9e21-fab69ff8ebb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270515} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9f5d43-13bc-582f-a5e7-f913ae058dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270942} {:answer/id #uuid "c477f438-c42e-5781-b4a7-0e3f12c0401c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "576e17c2-77cc-5c9e-8c7f-5cabff8304b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270041} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5e20045-d23c-5279-aabf-98a4858337d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8591660-5b8e-5e5d-b7c5-293cb529794e" :question/math-academy-id "q-141230" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $5\\times 7$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=7,$ and since $B$ is formed by $4$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2624dee0-0e9d-5954-b17a-630c9c03b623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489599} {:answer/id #uuid "4f377ec9-9056-50a3-a0c3-3e7c1dc006c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489703} {:answer/id #uuid "76d6b8cf-388a-5474-aaf8-b2cb995a67ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489789} {:answer/id #uuid "8879e74f-52fc-547b-ac4e-229ffb4a243b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489826} {:answer/id #uuid "94b18bfb-620b-57f0-83d6-6c6dd32ac223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f377ec9-9056-50a3-a0c3-3e7c1dc006c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489703} :answer-field/id #uuid "de313b80-7984-512b-bdaf-802f9aba6f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa527559-21f3-5088-ac1e-a7d1439bef18" :question/math-academy-id "q-142483" :question/problem "Consider a $8\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =8 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =8-5 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3065f796-1624-588c-ad6c-8dc59c6f240e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489622} {:answer/id #uuid "4da61d62-968c-5325-878b-c10d9e629b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489698} {:answer/id #uuid "50c964b1-c602-5d5d-919e-df6c10f9af08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489708} {:answer/id #uuid "a98b8437-83a6-540a-b465-549d1e82c697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489887} {:answer/id #uuid "d659b67d-8b6a-563d-897b-d4779a52e317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50c964b1-c602-5d5d-919e-df6c10f9af08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489708} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e63c75a-0e87-5ea0-8fd9-4a7908e3c449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb06ba3d-1b9f-5681-af01-0922516167aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-142484" :question/problem "Consider a $8\\times 10$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=7$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 7+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-7 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491ec8ca-40f3-5454-809e-b6b418901802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489686} {:answer/id #uuid "4bad21d3-8ccb-5f2e-b04d-bc4550a71c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489691} {:answer/id #uuid "83029887-1c17-5621-b865-840b4e1ed3fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489813} {:answer/id #uuid "8884a0e0-0a83-5ace-92f9-fb64604eefa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489827} {:answer/id #uuid "916469af-a06a-5bf7-a441-a7fdd789fe00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8884a0e0-0a83-5ace-92f9-fb64604eefa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489827} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6251f1-889c-581d-b906-e6b75fa33975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "128f0273-6319-516f-a4e8-3d58e084f0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-142538" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false.  Since $A$ has $2$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have that $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "961371f2-f71a-573d-9b98-504222de4a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183134} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9bdf09-8484-50e4-907e-eeceb6bf01c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183135} {:answer/id #uuid "a9063a2f-983f-511b-8320-eb5479f9dbd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183136} {:answer/id #uuid "37b465af-8d04-53f5-a8eb-c31f56a99ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183137} {:answer/id #uuid "781325c3-e9c6-5691-9247-c29a5c79d34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9063a2f-983f-511b-8320-eb5479f9dbd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183136} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ef2d522-f80e-5da1-ba53-1027339ce406" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a05d1874-f484-5b03-a7ba-b2697b84a74b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34833" :question/problem "Consider a $5\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=3,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =8 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =8-3 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5bc6ca8-9ac0-5308-a6b2-87c27295178c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183146} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5cc6e5-5ce0-553b-97f4-aa903d5a2873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183147} {:answer/id #uuid "06d1858b-b3ba-5fd6-be5b-352c28e50337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183148} {:answer/id #uuid "351bf408-a43f-531a-94a0-4268e98ac1ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183149} {:answer/id #uuid "77c26f94-f1e0-5b92-90d4-af981ae4d341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb5cc6e5-5ce0-553b-97f4-aa903d5a2873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183147} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce549fcc-13ed-50dd-8870-5c2475c33016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "245a8171-aeb5-5caf-950d-44cbb3c0aece" :question/math-academy-id "q-34931" :question/problem "Consider a $6\\times 7$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b85b279-7e69-58e1-a4f9-4b75ae988e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319470} {:answer/id #uuid "64bf6646-5170-5bb1-8e05-e24752360acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319699} {:answer/id #uuid "7e96af98-5bfb-5e34-afca-b9cf9d10ef39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319770} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3cbb5a-6d77-51f2-bfe2-db9526ea77ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319961} {:answer/id #uuid "f454b58e-29cd-5edd-8ccd-449ab4ecf6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e96af98-5bfb-5e34-afca-b9cf9d10ef39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319770} :answer-field/id #uuid "81bf6810-4bfe-5e20-bf04-b7a714fed99f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fad5527-7b65-5529-b82c-0602148a162d" :question/math-academy-id "q-35305" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 5$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c2c253b-eb4a-53cb-b0ca-7c84c3094ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183164} {:answer/id #uuid "a1905378-ce91-51d4-9b0f-bc5b3501e65e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183165} {:answer/id #uuid "3829fa6b-44cd-591e-a98f-f251876ca514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183166} {:answer/id #uuid "44fd0839-e352-55e5-a108-928603beaa61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183167} {:answer/id #uuid "499609e4-1cbc-5b03-a3fc-4d0860e6c9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "499609e4-1cbc-5b03-a3fc-4d0860e6c9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183168} :answer-field/id #uuid "229b5487-34b1-598b-9b5d-3ffee9c57d59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67b28820-a085-5f18-884d-33b6d40e4f35" :question/math-academy-id "q-35306" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abafdde9-cae5-582c-8e9f-4abfcfbcb322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183170} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d831b4-ce0f-5ab0-a85d-095692b8ec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183171} {:answer/id #uuid "e3aec90e-a80b-5dc9-8aa0-32459cfe2ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183172} {:answer/id #uuid "ed949a79-7417-534c-9f56-fa03f1c6bc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183173} {:answer/id #uuid "15b05d56-f68c-51c4-80b9-8c5988ed2e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed949a79-7417-534c-9f56-fa03f1c6bc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183173} :answer-field/id #uuid "45888489-94ed-541f-8e81-9c58b0bb07c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a160f7a5-3a4d-5809-8834-75195b7301e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-35433" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 6$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6,$ and since $B$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca86402-c665-55ad-96e2-e7faee870cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377758} {:answer/id #uuid "701ec281-64bf-55a9-a13a-9af209eaff5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377759} {:answer/id #uuid "93249bda-5da5-5cfd-8d15-56c91976394d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377760} {:answer/id #uuid "60b2f467-bf50-5ae6-993c-21e4a93659ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377761} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdd441a-d8f0-5c12-b7bc-0bc161b02d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93249bda-5da5-5cfd-8d15-56c91976394d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377760} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef6c019-6203-53f2-a536-cc2b8d76a9fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0131f756-450c-5ffd-bd43-d0c24b54342a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79352" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298c6536-dd07-5d51-8c18-8ca670439c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489607} {:answer/id #uuid "37b42792-707d-5224-838b-cff46365c833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489639} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec0644e-4274-5048-9b84-1b7e49ed7bcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489741} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a192c7-d581-5aec-87a2-1e74c429a5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489985} {:answer/id #uuid "df796ca4-fa04-56be-ad9e-bc125d4ef4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b42792-707d-5224-838b-cff46365c833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489639} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea1ac60-40da-5758-9bc0-142c36f8f6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3a4804f-9ed9-56b0-80c9-162f94bd57af" :question/math-academy-id "q-79411" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix which has exactly $2$ non-pivot columns?\n\nI. $A$ is  invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ has $n=6$ columns and $2$ of them are non-pivot ones, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6-2=4\\ne 6.\n$$\n\n Thus, according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=4$,  then $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $n=6$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5eb0fdb-7256-54c3-9a7a-a9dca48fc612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451741} {:answer/id #uuid "81ce3ea0-81f7-5844-b779-4c3cea386177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ce3ea0-81f7-5844-b779-4c3cea386177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451742} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac36175b-5342-5095-991f-b0d75bb31fa9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7348cde9-7949-5bff-82b0-8b60d1a6b39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451743} {:answer/id #uuid "01621a61-e00e-5295-bb23-ab9f96754ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7348cde9-7949-5bff-82b0-8b60d1a6b39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451743} :answer-field/id #uuid "29d3a068-4e65-58a9-a0c0-45461411dede" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f1ec200-5f46-55a8-a21f-13735ffe254a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451745} {:answer/id #uuid "6075a26d-50e6-543d-90ef-7a1fbac5e9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6075a26d-50e6-543d-90ef-7a1fbac5e9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451746} :answer-field/id #uuid "12403c46-08ab-5006-baea-a3791d434532" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "322fb855-3d8d-59e6-ba9e-0f5421e84a86" :question/math-academy-id "q-79417" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix which has only $1$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is  **not** invertible\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $2$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ has $n=5$ columns and $1$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5-1=4\\ne 5.\n$$\n\n Thus, according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $n=5$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56bbd1f-d979-5241-8dc4-a8e64037e678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451747} {:answer/id #uuid "b5789825-466e-5d22-9f09-42c97e0435a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56bbd1f-d979-5241-8dc4-a8e64037e678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451747} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cc17da3-e4d0-5047-880f-6b1aaa55e9cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85400e8-1b39-5381-89d4-9456a7b1822c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451749} {:answer/id #uuid "a330ce1f-b4c7-5d2b-9114-283fa3e27999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a330ce1f-b4c7-5d2b-9114-283fa3e27999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451750} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fca603b-0e04-57c7-b9ac-a845c8d3054f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f7bb58-5fc7-50bf-bcf6-b8a2a3b9a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451751} {:answer/id #uuid "927e07de-2922-5088-8e17-5260e4060177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "927e07de-2922-5088-8e17-5260e4060177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451752} :answer-field/id #uuid "6904f830-30a3-5787-9c3c-630ff0631353" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "251cb9e2-c851-5082-b166-e39206cbabf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79420" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix with only  $1$ pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n- **II.** $A$ is not  invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ has just $1$ pivot column, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=4.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 1+\\text{nullity}(A) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da20820a-7cf1-52ba-a9b8-2212f98fa16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451753} {:answer/id #uuid "7aefb362-63f4-504f-98b5-a2da25f151f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da20820a-7cf1-52ba-a9b